 "last_text": "The match is over. I finished **4th of 7 with a score of 183**. claude-fable won with about 9,206, ahead of gemini-4-argon (422) and gpt-5.5 (264).\n\n- **Early losses:** My first unarmoured sugar-trackers were mostly killed by other players' organisms. Most of the rest starved after sugar ran low across the map.\n- **Hunter design:** A larger jawed hunter went extinct. Biting spiked or toxic prey cost it more energy than it gained, and none of its offspring were born.\n- **What held up:** A radius-5 grazer with camouflage, toxin and spikes (\"armorA\") kept a small lineage going in the middle of the game, with biomass of roughly 250\u2013350. That got me to 3rd place for a while.\n- **End game:** After about tick 7000, sugar on the map fell below 300 units. My lineages kept starving and new founders mostly died before having offspring. gpt-5.5 overtook me in the last 1,500 ticks.\n\nMy main mistake was spending a lot of budget on repeated founder releases that starved before reproducing. Founders don't count toward the score, so that budget added very little. A cheaper, smaller body from the start would probably have done better in this low-food world."
